# The thread dump of debug and test builds (roadmap l4.md L2), on the AT's
# Sys Req key: every thread, its state and priority, and how much of its
# kernel stack it has used. The key arrives while the shell waits for it -
# for the reply of the OS server's thread, which waits in the kernel for
# the key (roadmap l4.md L6) - so the counter runs. The mouse's driver is
# still in the mouse's reset (roadmap l4.md L7).
program: shell
keys: {sysrq}
match: contains
---
rx286: thread root receiving priority 7, kernel stack used
rx286: thread printer receiving priority 6, kernel stack used
rx286: thread mouse awaiting a notification priority 6, kernel stack used
rx286: thread program awaiting its reply priority 3, kernel stack used
rx286: thread counter running priority 1, kernel stack used
rx286: thread os waiting priority 5, kernel stack used
rx286: thread os receiving priority 5, kernel stack used
